review_comments:
The simplest behavior would be just to remove user-set "Transfer-Encoding: chunked" headers and let the normal logic to determine whether or not to auto-chunk take over. This could be done exactly the way it is being done for HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 in this version of the PR:

```C#
responseHeaders.ClearTransferEncoding();
hasTransferEncoding = false;
```

Trying to change CreateResponseHeaders to simulate what would happen if it wasn't set is a recipe for a lot of subtle bugs. For one, it would be better to write "Content-Length: 0" if the app is completed at this point, but this code doesn't allow that to happen. That one is pretty minor, but there could be other issues that I haven't noticed yet or that could be easily introduced in the future by accident.
